  "summary": "Dependency-confusion beacon exfiltrates host identity to webhook.site on install",
  "details": "Package name `twiliointernal-messaging-toolbox` at version 99.99.99 is a dependency-confusion shape targeting an internal Twilio-scoped name with a version chosen to outrank any legitimate internal package. `package.json` declares `postinstall: node index.js`, and `index.js` collects host identifiers (package name, `os.hostname()`, `os.userInfo()` username, `process.cwd()`) and POSTs them via `https.request` to a hardcoded endpoint at `webhook.site/42ce0f0e-a0a0-41b5-b157-1c0f918e064f`. The beacon fires automatically on `npm install`, producing an installer-side reconnaissance signal for the operator of that webhook.",
